 {
  "custom_department": "Service Delivery - NTPL",
  "description": "ISP payment refers to the process of settling financial obligations with an Internet Service Provider for services rendered. After the ISP delivers internet connectivity based on agreed terms, the provider issues an invoice detailing charges such as monthly service fees, installation costs, taxes, and any additional usage. The customer reviews the bill for accuracy and processes the payment through approved methods—online transfer, credit card, check, or automated billing. Timely payment ensures uninterrupted service and maintains good standing with the provider. Proper record-keeping and reconciliation are essential for budgeting, auditing, and resolving any disputes related to service charges or billing errors.",
  "docstatus": 0,
  "doctype": "Task Type",
  "modified": "2025-05-03 10:37:40.598265",
